From bdc63776d7a06fb4fa1f28d6af90ca792006dfe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:19:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Retry with helpers inlined when a module reads a zero Private
 stand-in

When the emitter cannot trace a pointer, it defines a Private variable
initialised to OpConstantNull in its place. The module still validates,
so no retry tier runs, and every load through that pointer reads zero.
On macOS 27 this happens where a pointer crosses a helper call:

- Core Image's _ci_sampler_builder returns coreimage::Sampler_h with the
  sampler transform as a ptr addrspace(2) member. The kernel sampled at
  (0, 0), so the downsample and blur kernels behind System Settings'
  icons returned transparent black and the icons lost their symbols.
- CoreAnimation's narrow_blur_19 kernels read their offset table through
  a pointer parameter, and the A2Xghfc fallback shader read thousands of
  values the same way; the first window an app opened drew its toolbar
  black.

After translating, count the zero-initialised Private variables that are
loaded and never stored. When there are any, translate again from the
text with every non-recursive internal helper inlined and the aggregate
round-trips folded, and keep that result only if it reads strictly fewer.
Of 304 shaders from a macOS 27.2 boot, four read such a variable before
and none after; 299 translate to the same bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
